The summons are the problem, and they can be extremely nasty,
especially if you've never been the victim of one before.
Two umber hulks and three master mind flayers can ruin anyone's day,
especially if the appropriate escape methods aren't at your fingertips,
because, say, you've never done it before.  Yes, there are escape 
methods.  However, there's no guarantee the lich won't come after
you on, say, a no-teleport level.  It's easy to forget about the
E-word, and it's not 100% effective in any event.

Even if they don't kill you outright they can make a level unpassable.
There are ways and methods of dealing with hostile liches, of course,
but for an inexperienced player, I would avoid it as much as 
possible.  There's a reason they're high on most players' genocide
lists.
 
> If the op has means of escape, keep the arch lich. Seeing as this is 
